// induction from 1, for some k >= 1, wts in step
theorem: for all n >= 1, 2^n >= n + 1
proof
we proceed by induction on n.
base case n = 1: 2^1 = 2 >= 2.
inductive step: assume 2^k >= k + 1 for some k >= 1. wts 2^(k+1) >= k + 2
then 2^(k+1) = 2 * 2^k >= 2(k+1) by the inductive hypothesis
and 2(k+1) = 2k + 2 >= k + 2.
qed
